From df690b8be6f28f8a60a964cabbba711ba8fccc37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Moritz Angermann <moritz.angermann@iohk.io>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 16:07:42 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Model B: drive the v3 bytecode VM for hydra/flake jobsets
 (behind NIX_V3_DIRECT_EVAL)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Wire nix-eval-jobs' worker to the v3-native accessor surface
(nix-expr-v3 / include/v3/eval_jobs_api.hh) so v3 owns the heavy eval
while ALL store-side logic stays byte-for-byte unchanged.

Hypothesis killed (review round 2026-07-20): "gating on --flake covers
hydra." FALSE — hydra-eval-jobset invokes `--expr 'let flake =
builtins.getFlake (toString "<locked-url>"); in flake.hydraJobs or
flake.checks or (throw ...)'` and NEVER --flake (source-verified against
angerman/hydra@4c4d6fe5f). The gate now engages v3 for BOTH shapes:
  - --flake ref[#fragment] (CLI/manual), when lockFlags carry no
    --override-input/--update-input/--reference-lock-file (v3's internal
    re-lock cannot honor them -> tree-walker);
  - --expr with EMPTY autoArgs (hydra's shape) via v3::evalExprRoot;
    lambda/functor roots throw -> tree-walker fallback
    (autoCallFunction semantics).
Legacy jobsets (file positional / --arg) stay on the tree-walker.

Exact-parity per-job tree-walker fallback (jobNeedsTreeWalker, lazy TW
root evaluated at most once per worker):
  - aggregate jobs (_hydraAggregate) under --constituents — hydra passes
    --constituents ALWAYS; emitting empty constituents would create
    silently-green empty aggregates (the worst failure mode);
  - functor attrsets + lambda job values (TW's per-job autoCallFunction
    calls/unwraps them; MissingArgumentError parity included).

Error hardening: any exception escaping the v3 section rebuilds the
handle (reset-FIRST: the GcRoot dtor pops blindly LIFO) so the next job
gets a clean VMState; v3::CallDepthError maps to Response::Error
fatal=true (stack-overflow jobs abort the eval exactly like the stock
tree-walker's nix::StackOverflowError handling).

drv.cc: Drv::fromV3 forces name -> drvPath -> outputs (same field order
as fromPackageInfo, so errors surface from the same field); store-side
block byte-for-byte identical. meson: dependency('nix-expr-v3') +
cpp_std=c++23. default.nix: nixComponents.nix-expr-v3 in buildInputs
(the `nix build --override-input nix <v3-nix>` deploy route).

Gates (extended shadow jobset, 15 jobs: aggregate+constituents, functor,
defaulted/undefaulted lambdas, drv-in-meta/null-meta/path-meta, non-bool
recurseForDerivations, throwing job + continuation): parity OK in both
--force-recurse and plain modes vs the pristine-TW oracle; aggregate
carries both constituent drvPaths; worker continues after a failing job;
--select under a 1 MB nursery (the exitDepth==0 scavenge window) green.

