CR7-R1/CR8-R1: v3 is the fast path, the tree-walker is the correctness
oracle.  On ANY per-job v3 exception the worker rebuilds the v3 handle
and RETRIES that job on the tree-walker (unless NIX_V3_REQUIRE), so a
v3-vs-TW divergence can never make hydra wrong or worse-formatted —
worst case a divergent job is evaluated twice.  Subsumes the
numeric-segment / CA-output / non-attrset-meta / output-shape / error-byte
divergence classes surfaced by the round-2 review.

CR6-D4: v3 engagement now requires an empty applyExpr (--apply is a
tree-walker-only transform; engaging v3 under it would drop extraValue).
NIX_V3_REQUIRE read once as a static local.

