Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Round-3 review: conditional rebuild + env-flag value
 parsing

Three findings from the round-3 clean-room reviewers (empty-context, fable):

* rebuildV3 only on unexpected exceptions (RR7-C1 = RR8-R1 = RR6 = RR1-F4,
  four reviewers): a routine per-job eval error leaves the v3 VMState clean
  via the dispatch loop's exception barrier (clearBlackMarksOnException
  unwinds frames/valueStack/withStack to the synthetic outer frame and
  reverts in-flight thunks Blackhole->Suspended), so the handle is reused
  as-is. The full getFlake root-replay -- with a second live heap under
  GC_DONT_GC=1 -- is now taken only for a genuinely-unexpected exception
  type (helper v3StateCleanAfter: nix::BaseError + the v3-typed errors are
  clean). Removes the per-erroring-job cost on error-heavy jobsets.

* Value-parse NIX_V3_DIRECT_EVAL / NIX_V3_REQUIRE (RR1-F6 / RR3): 0/false/
  no/off => off. NIX_V3_DIRECT_EVAL=0 is now the in-place kill-switch; the
  prior presence-only check silently KEPT v3 engaged on "=0".

* #include <cstdlib>/<cctype> (RR9-3): std::getenv no longer relies on
  <stdlib.h> transitively hoisting it.

Also refreshes the rebuildV3 comment (GcRoot dtor now erases its own entry,
so reset()-before-rebuild is convention, not correctness).

Re-gated GREEN: patched nej links libnixexprv3 and engages; shadow parity
byte-identical to the pristine tree-walker oracle on the baseline flake and
on an extended flake (numeric "18" + malformed outputs) where the two new
v3 throws are retry-healed to exact TW output.

